---
title: "Rabbit hole"
note: "Powers of Ten as an endless loop: every clip finds a tiny detail (a dewdrop, a keyhole, a bird's pupil, a crack in a wall), dives into it, and the next clip bursts out of it into a different world at a different scale ($portal~1.out). One continuous macro-to-vast camera. Loop it on Motion Context with Run (Instant)."
tags: [loops, h3, reel, motion_context]
---
@h3 t2va 16:9
context: 22
style: live-action, cinematic macro and wide cinematography, photorealistic, one continuous unbroken ten-second shot
MUSIC: N/A

CHUNK the first world
$world = __world/landscapes__
$portal = __scale/portals__
SHOT 10s | push in, large, slow
The camera drifts through $world, then slowly lowers toward a tiny detail in it: $portal. It pushes closer and closer until the detail fills the frame completely and the camera passes into it.
SFX: $world.sfx; the sound narrowing to a hush as the camera closes in
HANDOFF: the camera dives into $portal

CHUNK the next world repeat forever
$world = {__world/landscapes__:2|__tour/rooms__}
$portal = __scale/portals__
SHOT 10s | push in, large, slow
$portal~1.out, and the camera is somewhere entirely different: $world, seen at a completely new scale. It drifts through it, then finds a tiny detail, $portal, and pushes in until the detail fills the frame and the camera passes into it.
SFX: $world.sfx; the sound narrowing to a hush as the camera closes in
HANDOFF: the camera dives into $portal
